# What `harv init` writes here, and what `harv sync` generates: symlinks into
# the Store, harv's record of which of them it owns, and the personal settings
# file that is nobody else's business.
#
# Two files in this project are deliberately absent from this list. `.claude/
# settings.json` carries the Tripwire, which only warns the teammate who clones
# the repository if it arrives with it. And `harvenv.lock` is what makes their
# Harvenv — and this repository's CI run — identical to yours.
.claude/skills/
.claude/.harv-materialized.json
.claude/settings.local.json
